# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Belt and braces.  Everything below is either live data, a credential, or
# notes that are mine and not the product's.  Most of it is already covered
# above; it is repeated here as whole directories so a new file dropped into
# one of them is ignored the moment it lands, rather than the first time
# somebody remembers to add a rule for it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Editor and tool directories.  Working notes and plans live in a local
# directory that is listed in .git/info/exclude instead of here, because the
# name of it has no business being in a file that ships.
.cursor/
.idea/
.vscode/

# Anything staged for a push, and the checksums that go with it.
shipping/

# Scan output, working clones and reports, by directory.
out/
outputs/
work/
workdir/
reports/
scan-output/
evidence/
artifacts/
tmp/
temp/
.cache/

# Databases and anything the app writes at runtime.
data/
db/
volumes/
backups/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-wal
*.sqlite3-shm
*.db
*.dump
*.bak

# Credentials, keys and certificates of every shape.
secrets/
.secrets/
credentials/
certs/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
*.crt
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
.netrc
.npmrc
secret_key
first-admin.txt


# The ship guard word list, and the link to it.  Site specific, never ships.
.ship-check.words

# Everything that is about building this rather than running it.
#
# Somebody downloading a scanner wants to run it.  They are not writing or
# debugging it, so the test suites and the fixtures they build are kept out of
# the release.  They live one directory over and work exactly the same there.
#
# The working notes directory is deliberately not named here.  Naming it would
# publish the one thing this file is trying not to say, so it is excluded per
# clone instead, in .git/info/exclude.
tests/

# Editor packages are built from ide/, never committed
ide/**/node_modules/
ide/**/*.vsix
